0,1,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
1,1,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
2,1,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We need a clear, rational system for this room. The current ""first-come, first-served"" approach is ambiguous and leads to unfairness regarding the cleanup.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree we need a purpose. However, I hope we consider how the space affects our interactions, not just the logistics of the furniture.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,"Let's be real, the room is a mess. But my biggest worry is who's actually doing the work to keep it running. I don't want more hidden chores.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,Let's stop the vague complaints. We're bleeding money on temporary fixes because this room fails its primary purpose. We need hard data on costs before we decide.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Peace is the foundation of productivity, my friends. Let us look at the environment with kindness and honesty so we can find a harmony that suits us all.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree on the data. We should look at the actual usage patterns and the physical state of the room to avoid arguing based on mere impressions.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, usage patterns are useful, but I'm also interested in where our most difficult conversations have happened. The environment shapes the dialogue.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, that's a bit poetic, but I'm looking at the clock. I want to know where the hours are going—whether it's walking or cleaning.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. Let's look at the invoices and the fit-out quotes. If we're paying for outside help, we might as well invest in a proper internal solution.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Servas,,"A room is more than its cost, Shunichi. It is a vessel for our energy. I believe we should examine the noise and the cleanliness.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"To be objective, we should investigate the tally of use and the state of the bins. That will show us who is using the space and who is neglecting it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I think we should also look at the partition wall. If we want a space for honest communication, we need to know how isolated we actually are.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,"I'm with Ryuji on the tally, but I'm more interested in the invoices for outside hire. I suspect we're paying people to do things we could avoid.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're finally thinking rationally. Let's get the financial figures and the fit-out quotes. I'm not signing off on a ""vibe"" without seeing the budget.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us not forget the sensory experience. I shall look into the partition wall and the crumbs, for the smallest details often cause the greatest unrest.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,It seems we are aligned on gathering evidence. I will focus on the usage data and the cleanliness to establish a baseline of responsibility.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will look into the partition wall and the history of our awkward conversations. I want to see if we have a place for the things that matter.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,May,,I'll handle the invoices and the round trip for lunch. I want to see exactly how much time and money is being wasted on logistics.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take the quotes for the fit-outs and the invoices. I want to compare the cost of the current inefficiency against the cost of a permanent fix.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Servas,,I will examine the partition wall and the crumbs and bins. Let us seek a solution that brings tranquility to those of us sitting nearby.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
