59,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the only one that solves the accountability problem. A booking calendar removes the ""first-come"" chaos and assigns responsibility for the room's state.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I find Option C acceptable only if the fit-out includes soundproofing. We need a place where we can have the conversations we've been avoiding for years.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm voting for Option A. The ""hidden cost"" of walking for lunch is a tax on our time that I'm tired of paying. Let's prioritize our well-being.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, well-being doesn't pay the invoices. Option C is the only choice that addresses the financial drain of external rentals. It's a professional necessity, not a luxury.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option C provides a structure that can maintain silence. If we treat it as a professional space, we respect the peace of those working nearby.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Jonathan, the fit-out quotes include a partition upgrade. Option C provides the most utility for the most people, as evidenced by the usage tally.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If the partition is upgraded, then Option C allows us to stop being strangers. It gives us a safe place to resolve conflicts without an audience.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"You're all ignoring the physical exhaustion. A kitchen isn't just about food; it's about having a place to actually breathe without feeling like we're still ""on the clock.""","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you can breathe in the park. You can't conduct a client meeting in the park. We are a business, and our space should reflect that. Option C is the only rational path.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"There is a certain wisdom in Shunichi's pragmatism, though I prefer the spirit of Jonathan's need for connection. Both are served by a quiet, professional space.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot support Option A because it would increase the cleaning burden and the noise. Option C is the most sustainable and fair system for everyone.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I've thought about it, and while I value the break, the lack of a private space for difficult conversations is a deeper wound. I'll vote for Option C.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"I feel like I'm the only one who cares that we're basically hiking for our lunch. But if you're all obsessed with the budget, I can't win this.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's not an obsession, May; it's basic accounting. We stop the external spend, we increase our internal capacity, and we professionalize the environment. Option C is the winner.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"When we create a space for focused intention, we create a space for growth. Option C will bring a necessary order to our shared chaos.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The consensus seems to be leaning toward Option C. It satisfies the need for data-driven utility, financial prudence, and a structured system of accountability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,As long as we use that space to actually talk to one another—honestly and privately—I am satisfied. Let's hope the room changes our culture too.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, have your meeting room. But don't come complaining to me when you're still exhausted from walking twenty-five minutes for a sandwich every day.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll take that risk. I'd rather be tired and profitable than rested and bankrupt. Let's put it to a vote and end this.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us move forward with a spirit of cooperation. Whether we eat or meet, the most important thing is that we do so with respect for one another.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
